\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. OMNIPOTENT Lord, my Saviour and King,
\par Thy succour afford, Thy righteousness bring:
\par Thy promises bind Thee compassion to have;
\par Now, now let me find Thee almighty to save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Rejoicingt in hope, and patient in grief
\par To Thee I look up for certain relief;
\par I fear no denial, no danger I fear,
\par Nor start from the trial, while Jesus is near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I every hour in jeopardy stand;
\par But though art my power, and holdest my hand:
\par While yet I am calling, Thy succor I feel;
\par It saves me from falling, or plucks me from hell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O who can explain this struggle for life
\par This travail and pain, this trembling and strife:
\par Plague, earthquake, and famine, and tumult, and war,
\par The wonderful coming of Jesus declare.
\par  
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 Yet God is above men, devils, and sin,
\par My Jesus's love the battle shall win;
\par So terribly glorious His comimg shall be,
\par His love all-victorious shall conquer for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.He all shall break through; His thruth and His grace
\par Shall bring me into the plentiful place,
\par Through much tribulation, through water and fire,
\par Through floods of temptation and flames of desire.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. On Jesus, my power, till then I rely,
\par All evil before His presence shall fly;
\par When I have my Saviour, my sin shall depart,
\par And Jesus for ever shall reign in my heart.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b  \f1\fs16 
\par 
\par }

